=== the window is [2026-09-12T10:00:00+01:00, 2026-09-12T12:00:00+01:00], 7200 s, interval 60

--- covered by sleep, with dark wakes too short to have run a tick
covering-sleep             {"assessed":"explained","sleep_seconds":7100,"longest_awake_seconds":50,"sleep_count":2}

--- the same history with the marker inside an awake stretch rather than a sleep: still short
awake-at-the-marker        {"assessed":"explained","sleep_seconds":7100,"longest_awake_seconds":50,"sleep_count":1}

--- a complete timeline with no sleep in the window at all
no-sleep                   {"assessed":"unexplained","sleep_seconds":0,"longest_awake_seconds":7200,"sleep_count":0}

--- overlap is not coverage: one awake stretch of exactly two intervals is not silent
exactly-two-intervals      {"assessed":"unexplained","sleep_seconds":7080,"longest_awake_seconds":120,"sleep_count":2}

--- and one second under it is
one-second-under           {"assessed":"explained","sleep_seconds":7081,"longest_awake_seconds":119,"sleep_count":2}

--- two short awake stretches are two opportunities, never one long one, and are not summed
two-short-stretches        {"assessed":"explained","sleep_seconds":6962,"longest_awake_seconds":119,"sleep_count":3}

--- a UTC offset change inside the window is read and never assumed. The wake below reads
--- 06:59:10 -0400, which is 11:59:10 +0100 and fifty seconds short of the endpoint; taking
--- the clock face at its word instead would put it five hours early and explain nothing.
offset-change              {"assessed":"explained","sleep_seconds":7150,"longest_awake_seconds":50,"sleep_count":1}

=== and every shape that is not a timeline. Unknown is not asleep: each of these keeps the
=== message and says which doubt it was, rather than claiming the host reported no sleep.

--- Wake Requests are scheduled requests and explain nothing on their own
wake-requests-only         {"assessed":"unknown","reason":"no-transitions"}

--- an empty history from a command that succeeded is not proof of no sleep
empty-history              {"assessed":"unknown","reason":"no-transitions"}

--- history that starts after the marker cannot say what the machine was doing when it began
no-state-at-marker         {"assessed":"unknown","reason":"no-state-at-marker"}

--- a Sleep at the boundary of the history with no wake after it: Baton is awake, reading this
trailing-sleep             {"assessed":"unknown","reason":"trailing-sleep-unmatched"}

--- a Sleep while already asleep is a wake the history lost, not twelve seconds of sleep
missing-wake               {"assessed":"unknown","reason":"missing-wake"}

--- but an unclosed stretch too short to have held a tick is an awake portion and not a doubt.
--- The real history carries twelve-second ones; reporting each as unknown would make a whole
--- night unreadable over a stretch that could not have changed the answer. It is still not
--- counted as sleep — 09:58 to 09:58:12 falls out as awake, which can only count against.
short-missing-wake         {"assessed":"explained","sleep_seconds":7128,"longest_awake_seconds":50,"sleep_count":2}

--- and the same for a Sleep at the end of the history, within two intervals of the endpoint:
--- unproven, so it is awake, and too short to be worth reporting as a doubt of its own
short-trailing-sleep       {"assessed":"explained","sleep_seconds":7140,"longest_awake_seconds":60,"sleep_count":1}

--- a doubt is positioned between the transitions either side of it, so one at the very start of
--- the history has nothing before it and one at the very end has nothing after, and each is
--- open on that side. The two ends therefore answer differently, which is the point of both
--- cases: a doubt open backwards is bounded forwards by the next good record, so a line that
--- would not parse a day before the window says nothing about the window --
malformed-first-line       {"assessed":"explained","sleep_seconds":7150,"longest_awake_seconds":50,"sleep_count":1}

--- -- while the same line at the end of the history is open forwards and bounded only by the
--- wake before it, so it could have happened inside the window and taints it
malformed-last-line        {"assessed":"unknown","reason":"malformed-timestamp"}

--- a conflict outside the window still disqualifies it when it is the record the state at the
--- marker is read from: the machine cannot have been both when the gap began
conflict-at-the-marker     {"assessed":"unknown","reason":"conflicting-transitions"}

--- asleep and awake at one instant is not a state
conflicting-transitions    {"assessed":"unknown","reason":"conflicting-transitions"}

--- a timestamp Baton cannot place is a hole, whether the month or the offset is the wrong one
malformed-offset           {"assessed":"unknown","reason":"malformed-timestamp"}

--- a reboot: the counter pmset prints per sleep cycle has gone backwards
boot-boundary              {"assessed":"unknown","reason":"boot-boundary"}

--- the clock moved backwards between two records, which no offset change can do
clock-discontinuity        {"assessed":"unknown","reason":"clock-discontinuity"}

--- a doubt outside the window says nothing about the window: the same reboot, a day earlier
boot-boundary-outside      {"assessed":"explained","sleep_seconds":7150,"longest_awake_seconds":50,"sleep_count":1}

--- and the read that failed, which is the plainest doubt of the lot
read-failed                {"assessed":"unknown","reason":"history-unreadable"}

